[{:adr/consequences "{:only_otete_orderable \"only Otete is actually orderable at this ADR's acceptance; a\\n                         per-character Hitogata biped remains aspirational until giemon's own\\n                         design track ships a real fixture/BOM\", :scale_is_followup \"the procurement pipeline's durability at scale (a real contracted EMS\\n                      relationship, live supplier onboarding, real shipment tracking) is a\\n                      business/operations follow-up, not built by this ADR\", :new_cross_repo_deps \"net-babiniku now depends on kotoba-lang/giemon and kotoba-lang/robotics\\n                        for anything touching a physical body -- real cross-repo dependencies,\\n                        not aspirational references\", :open_followup \"registering a net-babiniku-specific procurement actor (vs. reusing/forking\\n                 yoro-supply's cells directly) is an implementation decision left open\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["a net-babiniku persona may declare an associated physical Giemon body -- this ADR wires\n    existing Giemon products to character identities, it does not design a new robot" "only Giemon Otete (6-DOF arm + crawler, shipping, real BOM) is orderable under this ADR --\n    Hitogata (17-axis biped) remains :in-design with no articulation fixture and is NOT\n    presented as purchasable, per the honest-default principle" "any path from a persona's proposed behavior to a physical Giemon body's joint commands\n    must pass through kotoba-lang/robotics' safety gate exactly as kotoba.giemon.governor\n    already requires for Giemon Kaigo -- no LLM-to-actuator shortcut" "ordering/procurement reuses the yoro-supply Pregel-cell actor shape and cloud-itonami's\n    plm.cljc BOM primitives rather than building a new EC/ordering stack" "the robot purchase-order payment rail is a distinct, ordinary fiat rail from\n    ADR-2607062200's adult-content-gated chat-monetization rail -- must not be conflated"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "net-babiniku-giemon-embodiment", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607011000-cloud-itonami-robotics-premise-and-isic-21-21.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607020000-kotoba-lang-giemon-product-line.edn" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100-robotics-product-manufacturing-package.edn.edn"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607062210-net-babiniku-giemon-humanoid-embodiment-procurement", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-06", :adr/body "# ADR-2607062210: net-babiniku characters — optional physical embodiment via kotoba-lang/giemon, procurable through an EMS ordering pipeline\n\n## Status\nProposed\n\n## Context\n\nUser direction (2026-07-06): \"また キャラクターごとに kotoba-lang/giemon をベースに\nhumanoid ロボットも設計して, 発注できるようにして\" — also design a humanoid robot per\n`net-babiniku` character based on `kotoba-lang/giemon`, and make it orderable (発注できる状態\nに).\n\n### `kotoba-lang/giemon` — an existing open-hardware product line, not a green field\n\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/giemon/README.edn`: **Giemon** (ADR-2605142200) ships three products —\n**Otete** (6-DOF arm + crawler kit, `:product/status :shipping`, real articulation fixture at\n`fixtures/giemon_arm6/`), **Hitogata** (17-axis biped, `:in-design`, **no articulation fixture\nyet**), **Caterpillar** (dual-track UGV, `:in-design`). A fourth application, **Giemon Kaigo**\n(ADR-2605142300, in-home elder care), consumes these products but is a distinct use case from\nwhat's being asked here. The library owns product metadata, forward kinematics/torque\nvalidation, an actuator BOM generator (`arm/bom giemon-arm6 :all-qdd` /\n`:harmonic-shoulder`, ported from `kami-articulated-scene`), a viewer scene-IR, and CSV/JSON\nexport (`kotoba.giemon.export`). It explicitly does **not** own safety governance — that's\ndelegated to `kotoba-lang/robotics` (ADR-2607011000), and `kotoba.giemon.governor` is a thin\nwrapper over it.\n\n### `kotoba-lang/robotics` — the one safety contract every actuation path must go through\n\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/robotics/src/kotoba/robotics.cljc` (docstring, lines 1-17): \"the library is\npolicy, not control. It does not drive motors; it gives a governor the records it needs to\nrefuse unsafe actuation before it ever reaches hardware.\" `safety-classes`\n(`#{:none :low :medium :high :safety-critical}`), `human-sign-off-classes`\n(`#{:high :safety-critical}` require human sign-off / `interrupt-before`), `action-kinds`\n(`#{:sense :move :grasp :actuate :emit}` — only `:sense` is read-only). This is the same\ncontract all 26 `cloud-itonami` industry blueprints depend on (per giemon's own README, \"Why\"\nsection) — it is not something to route around for a new use case.\n\n### Real-machine control boundary and manufacturing-package precedent\n\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100-robotics-product-manufacturing-package.edn.edn`\n(Accepted): \"AI agent は actuator に直接 command を送ってはならない。... 実機送信は safety\ngateway が validation した後、asset-specific adapter へ渡す\" — the same non-negotiable\nboundary `kotoba.robotics` encodes. This ADR also defines the **manufacturing package**\nconcept for physical robot products: CAD/ECAD/CAM/BOM/routing/inspection/firmware/calibration\nbundled together, because \"この 1 ファイルを渡せば必ず作れる、という単一標準は存在しない\" for\nreal hardware.\n\n### Existing procurement/ordering actors — reuse, don't rebuild an EC stack\n\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/app-aozora/20-actors/yoro-supply/` (ADR-2605250850): a building-materials\n  procurement actor, five Pregel cells (`cells/{supplier_selection,order_placement,\n  manufacture_track,shipment,delivery_verify}.edn`), lexicon-typed PO/RFQ/manufacturing\n  progress/shipment/settlement events, 14 \"Constitutional Gates,\" input is a `projectBOM`.\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/src/itonami/{store,governor,kyber}.cljc`: `store.cljc`\n  line-items for procurement (UNSPSC/supplier/qty/cost); `governor.cljc` HARD-holds any\n  procurement item from an unregistered supplier (lineage-break invariant);\n  `cloud_itonami/plm.cljc` wraps `kotoba.plm.item` for `item`/`bom-edge`/`change-order`/\n  `make-buy`/`unit-cost`/`mbom-rows`.\n\nNo general-purpose EC/ordering stack exists in this repo, nor should one be built for this —\nthe actor-based procurement shape above is the established pattern for \"turn a BOM into a real\npurchase order.\"\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Physical embodiment is optional and per-character, not a new robot design.** A\n   `net-babiniku` persona may declare an associated Giemon body. This ADR does **not** design\n   a new humanoid — it wires existing (or eventually-existing) Giemon products to character\n   identities.\n\n2. **MVP orderable body = Otete (6-DOF arm + crawler), not Hitogata.** Hitogata (17-axis biped)\n   is the intuitively \"humanoid VTuber body,\" but it is `:in-design` with **no articulation\n   fixture** — there is no real BOM to order yet. Per the honest-default principle already\n   adopted in ADR-2607062200 (no fake checkout / no vaporware presented as purchasable),\n   **Hitogata is not orderable under this ADR.** Otete is real, shipping, and has a canonical\n   BOM (`fixtures/giemon_arm6/`) — it is what \"発注できるように\" can actually mean today. When\n   Hitogata's own design work (tracked independently under giemon/ADR-2605142200) reaches a\n   real fixture and BOM, it becomes eligible for the same ordering path with no changes to this\n   ADR's decisions — this ADR does not pull that design work forward.\n\n3. **No LLM-to-actuator shortcut, ever.** The persona/governor from ADR-2607062200 proposes\n   character behavior only (`dialogue`/`emotion`/`motion-cue`) for the *virtual* VRM body.\n   Any path from a character's behavior to a *physical* Giemon body's joint commands must pass\n   through `kotoba.robotics`'s `gate` exactly as `kotoba.giemon.governor` already requires for\n   Kaigo — `net-babiniku` gets no exception to `:high`/`:safety-critical` human sign-off, and\n   `:actuate`/`:move`/`:grasp`/`:emit` are never dispatched directly from a persona proposal.\n\n4. **Ordering reuses the yoro-supply Pregel-cell shape and cloud-itonami's `plm.cljc`\n   primitives**, rather than a new ordering stack: a per-character Otete BOM\n   (`arm/bom giemon-arm6 <realization-variant>`) becomes the `projectBOM` input to a\n   `supplier_selection → order_placement → manufacture_track → shipment → delivery_verify`\n   flow, packaged per ADR-2604252100's manufacturing-package manifest (BOM CSV via\n   `kotoba.giemon.export`, plus STEP/3MF/Gerber/inspection-plan as applicable) as the artifact\n   an EMS actually RFQs against.\n\n5. **Payment/fulfillment counterparty is separate from ADR-2607062200's chat-monetization\n   rail.** A robot purchase is an ordinary physical-goods fiat transaction with no\n   adult-content PSP constraint — it can use the org's existing Stripe-shaped billing schema\n   (`kotoba-lang/com-stripe`, `net-kotobase/billing.cljc` pattern) for the purchase-order\n   payment leg. This is intentionally a **different rail** from the paid-chat-tier decision in\n   ADR-2607062200; the two must not be conflated (one is adult-content-gated recurring\n   billing, the other is a one-time hardware PO).\n\n6. **Character↔body binding is a data association, not new engineering.** Which Giemon SKU\n   (today: only Otete) a persona \"owns\" as its physical embodiment is a persona-record field —\n   cosmetic/identity binding — not a new hardware variant per character.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Only Otete is actually orderable at this ADR's acceptance; a per-character Hitogata biped\n  remains aspirational until giemon's own design track ships a real fixture/BOM.\n- The procurement pipeline's *durability at scale* (a real, contracted EMS relationship;\n  live supplier onboarding; real shipment tracking) is a business/operations follow-up, not\n  something this ADR builds.\n- `net-babiniku` now depends on `kotoba-lang/giemon` and `kotoba-lang/robotics` for anything\n  touching a physical body — these become real cross-repo dependencies, not aspirational\n  references.\n- Follow-up: registering a `net-babiniku`-specific procurement actor (vs. reusing/forking\n  `yoro-supply`'s cells directly) is an implementation decision left open.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Design an all-new bespoke humanoid robot for net-babiniku instead of reusing giemon.**\n   Rejected — giemon is the existing open-hardware product line with real BOM/kinematics/\n   governor/manufacturing-package precedent; a bespoke design duplicates real engineering work\n   for no benefit, the same reasoning ADR-2607051800 already used to reject reimplementing VRM\n   rendering glue.\n2. **Let the persona governor command giemon joints directly (skip `kotoba.robotics`'s\n   gate).** Rejected — violates the repo's non-negotiable \"AI agent never commands actuators\n   directly\" doctrine (`kotoba.robotics` docstring, `itonami.governor`'s no-actuation\n   invariant, ADR-2604252100's safety-gateway requirement).\n3. **Build a bespoke EC/ordering system for robot purchases.** Rejected —\n   `yoro-supply`'s Pregel-cell procurement actor and `cloud-itonami/plm.cljc` already implement\n   this shape; reuse over reinvention.\n4. **Default to Hitogata (biped) as the flagship orderable body since it reads as more\n   \"humanoid\"/VTuber-appropriate.** Rejected — Hitogata is still `:in-design` per giemon's own\n   README, with no real BOM; presenting it as orderable would violate the honest-default\n   principle applied in ADR-2607062200.\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/giemon/README.edn`, `src/kotoba/giemon/{giemon,arm,kinematics,governor,\n  viewer,export,ui}.cljc`, `fixtures/giemon_arm6/`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/robotics/src/kotoba/robotics.cljc` (safety-classes, human-sign-off-classes,\n  action-kinds, gate contract)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100-robotics-product-manufacturing-package.edn.edn`\n  (real-machine control adapter boundary, manufacturing package definition)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607011000-cloud-itonami-robotics-premise-and-isic-21-21.edn`,\n  `90-docs/adr/2607020000-kotoba-lang-giemon-product-line.edn`\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/app-aozora/20-actors/yoro-supply/` (procurement Pregel cells, lexicons,\n  Constitutional Gates)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/src/{itonami/store.cljc,itonami/governor.cljc,\n  cloud_itonami/plm.cljc}` (procurement line-items, supplier-lineage HARD hold, BOM/PLM\n  primitives)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.edn` (sibling ADR —\n  the chat-monetization payment rail this ADR's PO payment rail must stay distinct from)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/com-stripe/src/stripe/main.cljc`,\n  `orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/clj-edge/src/kotobase/billing.cljc` (PO payment-leg schema\n  precedent)", :adr/decision "{:embodiment_scope {:what \"physical embodiment is optional and per-character, not a new robot design -- a\\n          net-babiniku persona may declare an associated Giemon body; this ADR wires existing\\n          (or eventually-existing) Giemon products to character identities\"}, :mvp_orderable_body {:what \"Giemon Otete (6-DOF arm + crawler) only, NOT Hitogata\", :why \"Hitogata is :in-design with no articulation fixture -- no real BOM exists to order.\\n         Per the honest-default principle from ADR-2607062200 (no vaporware presented as\\n         purchasable), Hitogata is not orderable under this ADR. Otete is real, shipping, and\\n         has a canonical BOM (fixtures/giemon_arm6/) -- that is what 発注できるように can\\n         actually mean today.\", :future \"when Hitogata's own design work (tracked independently under\\n            giemon/ADR-2605142200) reaches a real fixture and BOM, it becomes eligible for\\n            the same ordering path with no changes to this ADR's decisions -- this ADR does\\n            not pull that design work forward\"}, :no_actuation_shortcut {:what \"the persona/governor from ADR-2607062200 proposes character behavior only\\n          (dialogue/emotion/motion-cue) for the VIRTUAL VRM body. Any path from a character's\\n          behavior to a PHYSICAL Giemon body's joint commands must pass through\\n          kotoba.robotics' gate exactly as kotoba.giemon.governor already requires for Kaigo\\n          -- no exception to :high/:safety-critical human sign-off, :actuate/:move/:grasp/\\n          :emit are never dispatched directly from a persona proposal\"}, :ordering_pipeline {:reuse \"yoro-supply's Pregel-cell shape (supplier_selection -> order_placement ->\\n           manufacture_track -> shipment -> delivery_verify) and cloud-itonami's plm.cljc\\n           primitives, rather than a new ordering stack\", :mechanism \"a per-character Otete BOM (arm/bom giemon-arm6 <realization-variant>) becomes\\n              the projectBOM input to that flow, packaged per ADR-2604252100's\\n              manufacturing-package manifest (BOM CSV via kotoba.giemon.export, plus\\n              STEP/3MF/Gerber/inspection-plan as applicable) as the artifact an EMS actually\\n              RFQs against\"}, :payment_rail {:what \"ordinary physical-goods fiat transaction, no adult-content PSP constraint -- can\\n          use the org's existing Stripe-shaped billing schema (kotoba-lang/com-stripe,\\n          net-kotobase/billing.cljc pattern) for the purchase-order payment leg\", :must_stay_distinct_from \"ADR-2607062200's adult-content-gated chat-monetization rail --\\n                            one is adult-content-gated recurring billing, the other is a\\n                            one-time hardware PO; must not be conflated\"}, :character_body_binding {:what \"which Giemon SKU (today: only Otete) a persona 'owns' as its physical embodiment is\\n          a persona-record data field -- cosmetic/identity binding, not a new hardware variant\\n          per character\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-06: design a humanoid robot per net-babiniku character based\\n           on kotoba-lang/giemon, and make it orderable (発注できるように)\", :prior_art {:giemon {:what \"kotoba-lang/giemon (ADR-2605142200): open-hardware robot product line in pure\\n           Clojure -- product metadata, forward kinematics/torque validation, actuator BOM\\n           generator, viewer scene-IR, CSV/JSON export\", :products {:otete \":product/status :shipping, 6-DOF arm + crawler, real articulation fixture\\n             (fixtures/giemon_arm6/, EDN source of truth + URDF parity oracle)\", :hitogata \":in-design, 17-axis biped, NO articulation fixture yet\", :caterpillar \":in-design, dual-track UGV\", :giemon_kaigo \"ADR-2605142300, in-home elder-care application consuming these products --\\n                    a distinct use case from what's asked here\"}, :governance_delegation \"giemon does NOT own safety governance -- delegates to\\n                            kotoba-lang/robotics (ADR-2607011000); kotoba.giemon.governor is a\\n                            thin wrapper over it, per giemon's own README\"}, :kotoba_robotics {:what \"orgs/kotoba-lang/robotics/src/kotoba/robotics.cljc -- the one safety contract\\n           every cloud-itonami actuation path (26 industry blueprints) depends on\", :doctrine \"'policy, not control. It does not drive motors; it gives a governor the\\n               records it needs to refuse unsafe actuation before it ever reaches hardware.'\", :safety_classes \"#{:none :low :medium :high :safety-critical}\", :human_sign_off_classes \"#{:high :safety-critical} -- require interrupt-before human\\n                             sign-off\", :action_kinds \"#{:sense :move :grasp :actuate :emit} -- only :sense is read-only\"}, :manufacturing_package_adr {:what \"ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100 (Accepted): real-machine control\\n           adapter boundary + manufacturing package definition for physical robot products\", :control_boundary \"AI agent は actuator に直接 command を送ってはならない -- mission\\n                       plan/replan/approval/simulation only; real dispatch goes through a\\n                       safety gateway then an asset-specific adapter (ROS2/MAVLink/VDA5050)\", :manufacturing_package \"CAD/ECAD/CAM/BOM/routing/inspection/firmware/calibration bundled\\n                            together -- no single-file standard exists for real hardware\"}, :procurement_actors {:yoro_supply \"app-aozora/20-actors/yoro-supply (ADR-2605250850): building-materials\\n                  procurement actor, 5 Pregel cells (supplier_selection/order_placement/\\n                  manufacture_track/shipment/delivery_verify), lexicon-typed PO/RFQ events,\\n                  14 Constitutional Gates, input = projectBOM\", :cloud_itonami \"itonami/store.cljc (procurement line-items, UNSPSC/supplier/qty/cost),\\n                    itonami/governor.cljc (HARD-holds unregistered-supplier lineage breaks),\\n                    cloud_itonami/plm.cljc (item/bom-edge/change-order/make-buy/unit-cost/\\n                    mbom-rows via kotoba.plm.item)\", :conclusion \"no general-purpose EC/ordering stack exists or should be built -- the\\n                actor-based procurement shape is the established pattern for 'turn a BOM into\\n                a real purchase order'\"}}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"design an all-new bespoke humanoid robot for net-babiniku instead of reusing\\n            giemon\", :rejected_because \"giemon is the existing open-hardware product line with real\\n                      BOM/kinematics/governor/manufacturing-package precedent; a bespoke\\n                      design duplicates real engineering work for no benefit, the same\\n                      reasoning ADR-2607051800 already used to reject reimplementing VRM\\n                      rendering glue\"} {:option \"let the persona governor command giemon joints directly, skipping kotoba.robotics'\\n            gate\", :rejected_because \"violates the repo's non-negotiable 'AI agent never commands actuators\\n                      directly' doctrine (kotoba.robotics docstring, itonami.governor's\\n                      no-actuation invariant, ADR-2604252100's safety-gateway requirement)\"} {:option \"build a bespoke EC/ordering system for robot purchases\", :rejected_because \"yoro-supply's Pregel-cell procurement actor and cloud-itonami/plm.cljc\\n                      already implement this shape; reuse over reinvention\"} {:option \"default to Hitogata (biped) as the flagship orderable body since it reads as more\\n            'humanoid'/VTuber-appropriate\", :rejected_because \"Hitogata is still :in-design per giemon's own README, with no real BOM;\\n                      presenting it as orderable would violate the honest-default principle\\n                      applied in ADR-2607062200\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607062210: net-babiniku characters -- optional physical embodiment via\n          kotoba-lang/giemon, procurable through an EMS ordering pipeline", :adr/source-format "edn"}]